+        // ORDER MATTERS. This list is scanned with `notes.contains(pattern)` and
+        // breaks on the first hit, so any pattern that is a substring of another
+        // must come first. "half marathon" contains "marathon": with marathon
+        // listed first, every half marathon in the journal was recorded as a
+        // full one — a 1:28 half became a 1:28 marathon at 3:23/mi, passed the
+        // sanity check, and became the high-confidence fitness anchor that every
+        // pace zone in the app is derived from. Likewise "half" must precede
+        // "marathon", and "10 mile"/"half mile" must precede bare "mile".
         let distancePatterns: [(String, RaceType)] = [
-            ("marathon", .marathon), ("half marathon", .half), ("half", .half),
+            ("half marathon", .half), ("half-marathon", .half), ("half", .half),
