From e7a48dd10765dfcfb74d5e9dfa3304213ddb5579 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 6 Aug 2026 04:03:37 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 15/21] Fix 4.1 + 4.2 + 4.8: FIT header order, main-actor
 isolation, unbounded retry loop
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- FITExportService built every file with an invalid CRC and an oversized
  data-size field. The CRC was computed while the header's size field was
  still the 0x00000000 placeholder (patched afterwards), and the size was
  measured after the 2 CRC bytes had been appended, so it overstated the
  record section by 2. Garmin Connect rejected every export as corrupt,
  100% of the time. Header size is now patched first, CRC computed second.

- VoiceLogViewModel.loadHistory was the one mutating method on this
  @Observable class without @MainActor (the class itself isn't annotated).
  It ran on the cooperative pool and wrote six properties — driving SwiftUI
  invalidation off the main thread while the Log feed was laying out.
  Intermittent layout corruption and AttributeGraph crashes, worst during
  the 1-second processing poll while scrolling.

- autoRetryStaleRecords -> loadHistory -> autoRetryStaleRecords terminates
  only if the retry clears the stale row. A memo stuck at "transcribed"
  whose edge function short-circuits with success:true without advancing
  the status loops forever — a journal fetch plus a 60s function call per
  hop, for as long as the Log tab is open. Now one attempt per row per
  session.
---
 .../RunningLog/Shared/FITExportService.swift  | 20 +++++++++++----
 .../Workouts/VoiceLogViewModel.swift          | 25 ++++++++++++++++++-
 2 files changed, 39 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/RunningLog/RunningLog/Shared/FITExportService.swift b/RunningLog/RunningLog/Shared/FITExportService.swift
index 8ac5099..69ac042 100644
--- a/RunningLog/RunningLog/Shared/FITExportService.swift
+++ b/RunningLog/RunningLog/Shared/FITExportService.swift
@@ -71,15 +71,25 @@ final class FITExportService {
             data.append(contentsOf: createWorkoutStepMessage(step, index: index, racePaceSeconds: racePaceSeconds))
         }
 
-        // Calculate and append CRC
+        // ORDER MATTERS, and it used to be wrong in both directions.
+        //
+        // 1. Patch the header's data-size field FIRST. It counts the record
+        //    section only — header and CRC both excluded — so it must be
+        //    computed before the CRC bytes are appended. Doing it afterwards
+        //    overstated the section by 2.
+        // 2. THEN compute the CRC, over the finished header + records. The old
+        //    order CRC'd a header whose size field was still the 0x00000000
+        //    placeholder, so the checksum described a file that never existed.
+        //
+        // Between them, every .FIT this app produced was rejected by Garmin
+        // Connect as corrupt, 100% of the time.
+        let dataSize = UInt32(data.count - 14) // Records only: header excluded, CRC not yet appended
+        data.replaceSubrange(4 ..< 8, with: withUnsafeBytes(of: dataSize.littleEndian) { Data($0) })
+
         let crc = calculateCRC(data)
         data.append(UInt8(crc & 0xFF))
         data.append(UInt8((crc >> 8) & 0xFF))
 
-        // Update header with data size
-        let dataSize = UInt32(data.count - 14) // Exclude header
-        data.replaceSubrange(4 ..< 8, with: withUnsafeBytes(of: dataSize.littleEndian) { Data($0) })
-
         return data
     }
 
