MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- VitalManager's base URL was hardcoded to Junction's SANDBOX with no
  release override, so a TestFlight or App Store build queried sandbox and
  never returned a real workout. Now DEBUG-gated, with a VITAL_BASE_URL
  Info.plist override taking precedence.

- The Vital API key is NOT fixed here and cannot be fixed client-side: it
  is a server-side credential sitting in Info.plist, readable by anyone who
  unzips the .ipa. Left a prominent comment at the declaration. It needs to
  move behind an edge function and be rotated before any build leaves the
  machine — flagged rather than silently deferred.

- syncUnloggedWorkouts and AIInsightsService.fetchRecent both read
  AuthManager.userId, which returns "" with only a print warning when
  there's no session. Auto-sync fires at launch, often before the auth
  listener emits, so the dedup query matched nothing and the insert went
  out with user_id: "" — RLS rejected it and the athlete got a red error
  banner on cold launch. Both now use the same guard removeAutoSyncEntry
  in the same file already had.
