dedupedByPhysicalWorkout() clusters by distance, so a row with no mileage
never enters a cluster and never comes back out. That is correct for every
mileage aggregate — but it also meant the Train tab's voice-memo count
undercounted (five memos in a week could read as two) and mood(on:) could
never surface a non-running day, despite its own call site documenting
exactly that fallback.

The first attempt changed LogDedup to pass mileless rows through. That was
wrong: ~50 sites read the resulting `logs` array, and several count rows
or bucket them by intensity. A rest-day check-in would have inflated the
Runs stat, been listed under "Runs" in the pace-period drill-down, and —
because an empty ZoneSplit's hardestBucket is .easy — landed in the easy
bucket's session list. LogDedup is left exactly as it was.

Instead the view model keeps qualitative rows in a separate
`qualitativeLogs` array and reads it from precisely the three places that
want them: the voice-memo count, mood(on:), and weekMoodObservation().
Every mileage path is untouched.
